From c6e1afbee431fc6e6e8f001ca4412dea88312c9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Berkant Bakisli <berkant.bakisli@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 22:01:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] umd: accept pipelined raw frame streams

Repeated image inputs are decoded before execution, so they cannot represent
a continuing camera or video source. Add an opt-in raw frame stream input
backed by a bounded producer/consumer queue. The producer reads and converts
GRAY8 or BGR8 frames while the consumer executes the previous frame.

Record acquisition, preparation, queue, copy, execution, and output timings
without changing existing image behavior or the runtime library ABI.

Tested with the Buildroot AArch64 toolchain.

Signed-off-by: Berkant Bakisli <berkant.bakisli@gmail.com>
